00:45:28,660 --> 00:45:31,780
[EN]  What happens in adulthood and employment?

555
00:45:31,780 --> 00:45:35,500
[EN]  are accommodation and meaningful participation available

556
00:45:35,500 --> 00:45:38,440
[EN]  and beyond services altogether,

557
00:45:38,440 --> 00:45:42,980
[EN]  can people develop friendships, relationships,

558
00:45:42,980 --> 00:45:47,160
[EN]  belonging and meaningful roles in ordinary community life.

559
00:45:47,160 --> 00:45:50,420
[EN]  The studies by Westby and colleagues

560
00:45:50,420 --> 00:45:53,720
[EN]  and by Chen and colleagues also remind us

561
00:45:53,720 --> 00:45:57,600
[EN]  that access and service conditions can vary

562
00:45:57,600 --> 00:45:59,960
[EN]  by setting and local ecology.

563
00:45:59,960 --> 00:46:07,880
[EN]  So my point here, the slide, is that services are not that they are unimportant, quite the opposite.

564
00:46:07,880 --> 00:46:14,880
[ZH] 好服務是重要的,但服務並不保證你依照。

565
00:46:37,880 --> 00:46:39,340
[ZH] 還有青少年階段的時候

566
00:46:39,340 --> 00:46:41,620
[ZH] 這些支援資源可不可以跨場域

567
00:46:41,620 --> 00:46:44,880
[ZH] 跨體系持續幫助他們銜接還有陪伴

568
00:46:44,880 --> 00:46:46,520
[ZH] 以及等到他們成年以後

569
00:46:46,520 --> 00:46:49,820
[ZH] 職場還有社會是否具備合理的環境調整

570
00:46:49,820 --> 00:46:53,120
[ZH] 以及讓他們有實質的參與工作機會

571
00:46:53,120 --> 00:46:55,640
[ZH] 以及在社群和生活當中

572
00:46:55,640 --> 00:46:56,840
[ZH] 神經動向性的青年

573
00:46:56,840 --> 00:46:59,640
[ZH] 可不可以在社群中建立真實的人際關係

574
00:46:59,640 --> 00:47:01,040
[ZH] 獲得歸屬感

575
00:47:29,880 --> 00:47:36,280
[EN*]  we can think about some of the dimensions of community life can i enter here

576
00:47:38,840 --> 00:47:46,200
[EN]  can i function here without unnecessary barriers can i take part meaningfully am i

577
00:47:46,200 --> 00:47:52,760
[EN]  recognized as a valued member can i matter here now this should not necessarily be understood as

578
00:47:52,760 --> 00:47:58,360
[EN]  rigid stages someone can have access without participation someone can participate without

579
00:47:58,360 --> 00:48:22,360
[EN]  the feeling that they belong, and contribution does not mean economic productivity, it can mean that the person's presence, relationships, perspectives, care, or participation has value within shared community life, so the goal here is not simply inclusion by physical presence, but it is community membership.

580
00:48:00,040 --> 00:48:14,040
[ZH] 而,貢獻並不是經濟的充足,而是人的身份,關係,觀眾,關係,關係,關係,關係,關係,關係,關係,關係,關係,關係。

581
00:48:14,040 --> 00:48:22,040
[ZH] 所以,這個目的目的,不是單純的充足,而是社會的充足。

582
00:48:22,040 --> 00:48:25,140
[ZH] 那所以就是社群心理學

583
00:48:25,140 --> 00:48:29,160
[ZH] 其實它有更多樣的這個面向去討論

584
00:48:29,160 --> 00:48:33,900
[ZH] 比如說就是我們可以在這裡做我自己嗎

585
00:48:33,900 --> 00:48:35,960
[ZH] 我可以好好的參與嗎

586
00:48:35,960 --> 00:48:37,000
[ZH] 我屬於這裡嗎

587
00:48:37,000 --> 00:48:39,440
[ZH] 我可以發揮我的作用嗎

588
00:48:39,440 --> 00:48:40,580
[ZH] 發揮我的價值嗎

589
00:48:40,580 --> 00:48:45,700
[ZH] 那所以這些並不是用一個很僵化的階段去理解的

590
00:48:45,700 --> 00:48:50,020
[ZH] 就是有些人呢可以獲得參與感

591
00:48:50,020 --> 00:48:54,340
[ZH] 那有些人呢是需要有歸屬感

592
00:48:54,340 --> 00:48:57,280
[ZH] 所以這些貢獻並不表示說

593
00:48:57,280 --> 00:49:01,320
[ZH] 是否對社會做出貢獻並不表示說

594
00:49:01,320 --> 00:49:02,400
[ZH] 一定是可以賺錢

595
00:49:02,400 --> 00:49:06,200
[ZH] 或是在經濟上面有做出生產力

596
00:49:06,200 --> 00:49:10,620
[ZH] 這意味的是這個人他有沒有價值感

597
00:49:10,620 --> 00:49:13,500
[ZH] 存在感好好的發展出他人的關係

598
00:49:13,500 --> 00:49:15,620
[ZH] 他的觀點是否被重視

599
00:49:15,620 --> 00:49:17,400
[ZH] 他能不能得到很好的關懷

600
00:49:17,400 --> 00:49:31,400
[ZH] 那所以我們的目標就並不只是在生理或是物理上面接納一個人,而是要讓他真正成為一個社群的成員,讓他有心理上面的歸屬感。

601
00:49:40,360 --> 00:49:46,280
[EN]  Now, let me end with the only phrase, with the rules of laws.

602
00:49:46,700 --> 00:49:49,600
[EN]  There's no home, there's no place like home.

603
00:49:50,760 --> 00:49:53,920
[EN]  Home, in this sense, is more than a place where we are allowed to enter.

604
00:49:54,400 --> 00:50:00,580
[EN]  It is a place where we can participate, where we are known, where we belong, where we matter.

605
00:50:01,100 --> 00:50:07,160
[EN]  And for many years, for many years, autism intervention has understandably asked,

606
00:50:07,780 --> 00:50:14,300
[EN]  How can we help autistic people become better prepared for school, work, relationship, and community life?

607
00:50:14,900 --> 00:50:16,960
[EN]  We should continue asking that question.

608
00:50:18,140 --> 00:50:22,540
[EN]  But I would like us to place a second question right beside it.

609
00:50:23,400 --> 00:50:31,800
[EN]  That is, how can schools, workplaces, clinics, families, and communities become better prepared for autistic people?

610
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:36,380
[EN]  The future of autism support, I believe, depends on both.

611
00:50:37,080 --> 00:50:42,860
[EN]  not treatment without dignity, not acceptance without needed support,

612
00:50:42,860 --> 00:50:46,600
[EN]  not individual education without environmental responsibility,

613
00:50:46,600 --> 00:50:55,580
[EN]  but an approach in which people can receive the support they need and at the same time participate, belong, and matter.

614
00:50:55,580 --> 00:51:01,360
[EN]  So perhaps the final question that you and I have to ask is very simple.

615
00:51:08,600 --> 00:51:14,600
[ZH] 我最後想用綠眼仙中的明言作解,沒有地方比得上家,

616
00:51:14,600 --> 00:51:19,600
[ZH] 家在這個層面來說,並不是形式上的家庭,

617
00:51:19,600 --> 00:51:23,900
[ZH] 而是一個我們可以讓名詞接納還有進入的地方

618
00:51:23,900 --> 00:51:26,340
[ZH] 讓每個人有參與感的地方

619
00:51:26,340 --> 00:51:29,500
[ZH] 讓我們覺得有歸屬感和發揮價值的地方

620
00:51:29,500 --> 00:51:35,840
[ZH] 所以我們常常會想要介入自閉症患者的方式是

621
00:51:35,840 --> 00:51:38,440
[ZH] 我們要怎麼樣幫助自閉症患者

622
00:51:38,440 --> 00:51:43,400
[ZH] 可以更好準備面對學校工作還有關係還有社群與生活

623
00:51:43,400 --> 00:51:45,640
[ZH] 那現在我覺得我們應該也要問說

624
00:51:45,640 --> 00:51:51,120
[ZH] 我們學校、工作場域還有診所、家庭、社群

625
00:51:51,120 --> 00:51:58,080
[ZH] 可以怎麼樣來調整來更好準備為這些致病療症患者服務

626
00:51:58,080 --> 00:52:03,720
[ZH] 所以這個很重要的就是所有的治療都應該要讓人有尊嚴感

627
00:52:04,040 --> 00:52:06,440
[EN*]  And everyone needs to be trusted.

628
00:52:06,440 --> 00:52:09,240
[EN*]  So, the final question is very simple.

629
00:52:09,240 --> 00:52:14,020
[EN*]  I can do it here, I can participate in it, I can have a value in it, I can have a value in it.

630
00:52:16,660 --> 00:52:20,320
[EN*]  So, ladies and gentlemen, thank you very much for listening.

631
00:52:20,320 --> 00:52:23,320
[EN*]  Thank you very much for listening.

